  "59": {
    "inputs": {
      "prompt": "subject_definitions: <Picture 1> is the uploaded 地理 reference at order 1. <Subject 1> is the early-1900s Greenwich Village top-floor artist studio in <Picture 1>, with a narrow iron bed, a tall rain-streaked window, exposed brick, faded curtains, and period furniture. <Picture 2> is the uploaded 身份 reference at order 2. <Subject 2> is Johnsy in <Picture 2>, with a pale young woman with a short tousled dark-brown bob and the project's pale ivory nightdress continuity. <Picture 3> is the accepted opening frame for [Shot 1], fixing the approved starting composition, visible positions, and initial state for this shot. <Audio 1> is the uploaded voice-timbre reference for 约翰茜说话时的音色、声线和稳定身份识别; it stabilizes voice identity only and is not copied as dialogue, room tone, or music.\nsummary: [keyframe completion + reference generation + audio reference] The target video is a single vertical period-drama shot in the early-1900s New York artist-apartment world. Johnsy counts the falling leaves from her bed and keeps her face turned toward the window. The opening is anchored by <Picture 3> and preserves <Subject 1>, <Subject 2>.\nretention_analysis: <Picture 1> (reference image order 1): fully_preserved - its 地理 role is retained as the input reference for this shot. <Picture 2> (reference image order 2): fully_preserved - its 身份 role is retained as the input reference for this shot. <Picture 3> (opening frame of [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the supplied starting composition, visible placement, and initial state open the shot. <Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - a narrow iron bed, a tall rain-streaked window, exposed brick, faded curtains, and period furniture remain stable; the approved motion changes only the shot's stated action and endpoint. <Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - a pale young woman with a short tousled dark-brown bob and the project's pale ivory nightdress continuity remain stable; the approved motion changes only the shot's stated action and endpoint. <Audio 1> (voice-timbre reference for Johnsy S1): reference - used only to stabilize the corresponding speaking voice; not copied as speech content, room tone, or music.\ndetailed_description: The target video is a realistic live-action period drama in a vertical 9:16 frame, with restrained natural light, tactile period materials, and observational camera movement. The shot begins from <Picture 3>, with <Subject 2> lying on the narrow bed inside <Subject 1>. At 0.00 to 1.60 seconds her eyes remain fixed toward the window and she quietly starts counting. Johnsy (S1), using the voice timbre referenced from <Audio 1>, says: <d>[Chinese] 五……</d> At 1.60 to 3.70 seconds wind crosses the window and one leaf drops in the background; her eyes follow the falling point without turning toward Sue. At 3.70 to 5.80 seconds she continues using the voice timbre referenced from <Audio 1>, in the same low voice: <d>[Chinese] 四。</d> The camera makes only a very small slow push toward her profile and holds the accepted ending with four leaves behind her. The movement is one continuous take with no cut. No non-diegetic subtitles, captions, or dialogue text overlays appear at any moment. Continuity locks: pale ivory cotton nightdress; narrow top-floor artist studio with a tall rain-streaked window and exposed brick; final olive-green leaf on a wet brown vine.\noverall_soundscape: Damp window room tone, a restrained gust against the glass, one faint leaf flutter, and Johnsy's quiet breath around the spoken count.\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A"
    },
